If a patient receives a benzodiazepine and a clinician plans a benzodiazepine-discontinuation that stops the benzodiazepine for the patient then the clinician should gradually taper the benzodiazepine before the benzodiazepine-discontinuation.
Every abrupt-benzodiazepine-withdrawal can relate to a rebound-anxiety and can relate to a hallucination and can relate to a seizure and can relate to some delirium-tremens and can rarely relate to a death.
